__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.nbc
*.nbi
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.venv/
venv/
build/
benchmarks/cec_suite_cpp/build/
dist/
*.egg-info/
!results/
# Smoke-rehearsal output of scripts/run_revision_experiments.py --smoke.
# Truncated budget, tiny function set: it is NOT evidence and must never be
# promoted or committed. Campaign staging under results/_revision/ is ALSO
# ignored -- see the D-0049 block below; the tracked, citable evidence is the
# promoted release under benchmarks/cec_reference_results/_revision/.
results/_revision_smoke/
# Diagnostic re-execution staging (D-0051). Re-runs already-released cells to
# answer a provenance question; it is a MEASUREMENT, not new evidence, and every
# cell it produces is deterministically regenerable from the recorded seeds. It
# must never be promoted or cited. Note that results/ is deliberately NOT
# blanket-ignored -- results/_run_all/ IS tracked -- so a diagnostic tree left
# unnamed here would be swept in by `git add -A`.
results/_g1_recheck/
# Revision-campaign staging curves: one representative convergence CSV per
# (function, dimension), deterministic-regenerable from recorded seeds (same
# rationale as DTTrace_*.jsonl). The promoted release under
# benchmarks/cec_reference_results/_revision/ excludes them by manifest.
# NOTE: now redundant -- the D-0049 block below blanket-ignores results/_revision/,
# and `git check-ignore -v` attributes the match to that later, broader rule. Kept
# deliberately: it documents WHY the curves are excluded, and it keeps working if
# the blanket rule is ever narrowed.
results/_revision/*/dt-gsk/cec2017/curves/
# Raw DT-GSK per-generation diagnostics traces: deterministic-regenerable bulk
# (seeds recorded in run_config/seed_schedule; single files can exceed GitHub's
# 100 MB limit). The derived diagnostics_analysis CSVs stay tracked.
DTTrace_*.jsonl
# LaTeX build intermediates (papers/); the curated *_missing.log provenance
# files are kept tracked.
papers/*.aux
papers/*.bbl
papers/*.blg
papers/*.out
papers/*.toc
papers/*.log
!papers/*_missing.log

# Reference-paper PDFs are copyrighted acquisition targets, not committed evidence
# (the reference_papers/README.md index + references.bib are tracked; PDFs are not).
reference_papers/*.pdf
# ...and recursively. The line above is a SINGLE-LEVEL glob: it cannot cross a
# '/', so it never matched reference_papers/Academic_Research_Guidelines/ and
# seven copyrighted PDFs (38.8 MiB) reached the public remote, where they stayed
# from 2026-08-07 until they were removed (D-0049).
reference_papers/**/*.pdf

# --- Withheld from the repository entirely (D-0049) --------------------------
# Confidential peer review. Both round-one reviewers declined to sign;
# republishing their reports is the journal's act at acceptance, in the
# journal's own form, not the authors' act mid-revision. The response letter is
# withheld with them because it reproduces both reports verbatim. All three stay
# on disk for the authors and are retained in git only on the never-pushed
# branch archive/revision-pass-39-full.
# DENY BY DEFAULT, then allow back the one file that must stay public. The
# previous form listed the three withheld files by exact name, which is an
# ALLOW-by-default rule wearing a deny's clothing: any reviewer artifact added
# later - a second reviewer's PDF, a revised report, an editor letter - landed
# unignored and one `git add -A` from being published. That is the same failure
# shape as the `reference_papers/*.pdf` glob that never matched a subdirectory
# and put 38.8 MiB of copyrighted PDFs on the public remote. Verify additions
# with `git check-ignore -v <path>`, never by reading the pattern.
papers/review_2026_08_24/**
# NOT ignored, deliberately: revision_experiments_preregistration.md. It is the
# authors' own document, quotes no reviewer, and is what the Supplementary
# Materials' pre-registration claim depends on being checkable.
!papers/review_2026_08_24/
!papers/review_2026_08_24/revision_experiments_preregistration.md

# Co-author material supplied privately, including two biographies marked in the
# file itself as awaiting their subjects' approval.
papers/submission/AUTHOR_DATA_HANDOFF.md

# Revision-campaign staging output: a superset of the promoted, manifest-hashed
# release at benchmarks/cec_reference_results/_revision/ (which IS tracked and
# published in full), plus console logs and a driver log.
results/_revision/
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# build lock-workaround temp (build_pdf.py writes this when DT-GSK.pdf is open)
papers/DT-GSK.new.pdf

# standalone TikZ compile intermediates (source .tex + final .pdf are kept)
papers/figures/concept/*_src.pdf
papers/figures/concept/*_src.aux
papers/figures/concept/*_src.log

# latexmk build-state byproducts (embed machine-local absolute paths; builds
# go through papers/scripts/build_pdf.py — panel round-2 finding S4-9)
*.fls
*.fdb_latexmk
# stale editor/backup droppings (round-2 finding S4-4)
.bak
*.bak

# agent/tool session state (never publish)
.claude/

# Visio OLE build product (C-001 5.4: never commit; regenerate with
# papers/scripts/embed_visio_ole.py). Committed once by accident 2026-08-01.
papers/DT-GSK_visio.docx

# Change-marked manuscript for MDPI check-list item (II). Derived: rebuild with
# papers/scripts/build_change_marked_pdf.py, which diffs v2.13 against the
# submitted tag. Not committed, for the same reason the change register is not:
# it is a rendering of the tagged diff, and the tags are the record.
papers/submission/DT-GSK-changes-marked.pdf
# Change register, same reasoning; rebuild with
# papers/scripts/build_change_register.py
papers/submission/DT-GSK-change-register.pdf
papers/submission/DT-GSK-supplementary-changes-marked.pdf
# Response-to-reviewers PDF, staged here for the SuSy upload. NEVER commit:
# it quotes both reviewer reports verbatim (D-0049). Canonical source is
# papers/review_2026_08_24/response_to_reviewers.md (also withheld);
# re-render with the pandoc command recorded in SUBMISSION_KIT.md.
papers/submission/response_to_reviewers.pdf
papers/submission/response_to_reviewers.docx
papers/submission/DT-GSK-marked-and-register.zip
# Email-staged copy of the clean supplement under the journal's own filename
# (pass-64, 2026-09-01): byte-identical to papers/supplementary.pdf, which is
# the tracked, freeze-hashed original. A staged duplicate is never committed.
papers/submission/algorithms-4507562-supplementary.pdf
papers/submission/EMAIL_DRAFT_supplement_resend.md
# Graphical abstract (2026-09-01, editorial request): derived, regenerable
# with papers/scripts/build_graphical_abstract.py (tracked).
papers/submission/DT-GSK-graphical-abstract.png
# Supplement sources zipped for the editorial office (2026-09-02): derived and
# regenerable with papers/scripts/build_supplement_source_zip.py (tracked),
# which verifies the archive recompiles on its own before writing it. The
# two algorithms-4507562-* files are email-staged copies under the journal's
# filenames, byte-identical to the tracked originals.
papers/submission/DT-GSK-supplement-latex-source.zip
papers/submission/algorithms-4507562-supplementary-latex.zip
papers/submission/algorithms-4507562-supplementary.docx
